Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 22:22:50 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 68/71] Raise the per-call tool output cap from 10k to 25k
 tokens

Measured on the `wire` task (read 44 .rs files under codex-api/src, write WIRE.md), fork alone,
same relay, same prompt:

  cap 10,000   26 requests   2 compactions   $0.0310
  cap 25,000   18 requests   1 compaction    $0.0177   (-43%)

The 10k cap was binding hard: 6 of 29 tool outputs carried a truncation marker and the largest sat
pinned at 10,053 tokens. The model batches its reads already - `Get-Content a; '---'; Get-Content b`
- and the cap was cutting the tail, so it kept batches to three to six files. Every extra read turn
re-sends the whole window, the window then reaches the 70k compaction limit, compaction destroys
every tool output, and the model re-derives with `rg` what it had already read. Five consecutive
search-only turns after the first compaction were exactly that.

Raising the cap breaks the loop at its entry: bigger batches, fewer turns, the window reaches 70k
once instead of twice. It does not invite runaway outputs - at 25k the largest output settled at
~11k and only one of 17 was truncated, so the model takes the room it needs and no more.

The deliverable is unchanged: 44 file:line citations, all 44 resolving to real lines.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 codex-rs/models-manager/models.json | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/codex-rs/models-manager/models.json b/codex-rs/models-manager/models.json
index 227d379eff..8e20b97a13 100644
--- a/codex-rs/models-manager/models.json
+++ b/codex-rs/models-manager/models.json
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@
       "supports_image_detail_original": false,
       "truncation_policy": {
         "mode": "tokens",
-        "limit": 10000
+        "limit": 25000
       },
       "supports_parallel_tool_calls": true,
       "tool_mode": null,
